            "review_title": "Review at Chef Mamma's",
            "review_text": "Allosauridae Bolla\nLiverpool, United Kingdom27 contributions\n1\nExtremely poor\nJan 2020 • Couples\nThe menu was impressive so we decided to go in for some pizza.\nThey weren't doing pizza because it was lunar new year.\nThey weren't doing starters because it was lunar new year.\nWhy open in the first place if only half your menu is unavailable? But, my partner and I had walked a long way to get here, so we reluctantly stayed.\nWe both ordered the 4 cheese spaghetti and it was unacceptable. There was no seasoning and the presentation looked like something you'd make for a child in about 10 minutes. It also wasn't 4 cheeses, it was a bland, flavourless cheese sauce. Finally, the chips we ordered had no salt and were cold.\n\nP.s in a bizarre twist, a family entered the restaurant and one of the children started to vomit all over the floor. This can't be helped and I appreciate that sometimes this happens. What I can't forgive is how the staff stood there and watched this poor kid being sick all over the floor. Nobody went to get a bucket and nobody went to get a mop to clean it up either. Everyone just stood around and left the sick all over the floor.\n\nI do feel as though we came to this restaurant at an awkward time (lunar new year) but if you're open, shouldn't you provide everything on the menu? A less than satisfactory visit.\nRead more\nWritten January 22, 2020",
